# Narration align lock (do not regress)

Anthony (2026-11-02): Steam Cracker spoken audio often did not match Edit Slide → Audio or the Review script on slides he had not edited. Regenerating the slide re-recorded from the box and “fixed” it.

`npm test` must stay green (`src/lib/narrationAudio.test.ts`).

## Invariants (code, not comments)

- **TTS speaks the Audio box.** [`slideNarrationScript`](src/lib/narrationAudio.ts) / [`tabNarrationScript`](src/lib/narrationAudio.ts) use `voiceOverText || narration` only. Do not fall back to OST, nested item copy, or a title placeholder — that records a clip the Audio box does not show.
- **Applying a clip stamps the script.** [`applyJobResults`](src/hooks/useTTSGeneration.ts) writes `voiceOverUrl` **and** the job `text` onto the slide/tab.
- **Background QC cannot rewrite narration.** [`autoFixCourse`](src/services/qcService.ts) skips issues where [`qcFieldTouchesNarration`](src/lib/qcTextFix.ts). Manual QC still can, and still prompts to regenerate audio.
- **Merge keeps clip + script.** [`mergeCoursePreservingAudio`](src/lib/narrationAudio.ts) keeps `voiceOverUrl` **and** `voiceOverText` when a later imagery/QC commit has no new clip. Do not restore “keep URL, take the new script.”
- **Chrome VO is one string.** Player tour / objectives / hub / cover defaults in [`App.tsx`](src/App.tsx) match the TTS synthetic job via `PLAYER_TOUR_NARRATION`, `COURSE_OBJECTIVES_NARRATION`, `HUB_MENU_NARRATION`, `defaultCoverNarration`. Module overview defaults stay “Let’s revisit the objectives for this module.”
- **Chrome clips record first.** [`buildCourseNarrationItems`](src/hooks/useTTSGeneration.ts) queues synthetic cover / tour / objectives / hub / module title / module overview jobs **before** teaching slides so a dropped TTS run still speaks every Audio-box chrome slide. `onlyMissing` skips synthetics that already have a live URL (`collectSyntheticNarrationJobs` passes `voiceOverUrl`). Do not append chrome jobs after the last teaching slide.
- **Player tour waits for Show Me.** Narration for `__player-tour__` stays silent until [`PlayerTourSlide`](src/components/player/PlayerTourSlide.tsx) `onShowMe`. Skip does not play the tour VO.
- **Process/tab Overview audio is separate.** Edit Audio can generate the main slide clip without looping tab jobs (`Generate Overview audio` / `Generate Instruction audio`). `Regenerate Audio for this Slide` still does main then every tab.
- **Manual edits still need Generate.** Changing the Audio box does not re-speak until the author clicks Regenerate audio.
- **A clip follows its slide id.** Persist and restore narration as `slide:{id}` / `tab:{slideId}:…` / `synth:{id}`. Do **not** attach leftover `modules[i].slides[j].voiceOverUrl` blobs — after Add content those slots belong to a different slide (3.9 was playing 3.12). [`applyNarrationUrls`](src/lib/draftMedia.ts) / [`attachHeavyMedia`](src/lib/draftMedia.ts) skip [`isIndexKeyedAudioPath`](src/lib/draftMedia.ts). [`mergeDraftAssetPaths`](src/lib/draftMedia.ts) drops leftover index audio. [`harvestPlayerAudio`](src/lib/narrationCache.ts) only saves when the `<audio>` src equals that slide’s URL. [`ensureUniqueSlideIds`](src/lib/courseSlideEdits.ts) on generate and draft open. `npm test` must stay green (`src/lib/draftMedia.test.ts`).
- **A tab clip stays on that tab.** Player playUrl uses [`playbackUrlForSlide`](src/lib/narrationAudio.ts) so a process/tab MP3 cannot play on the next click-reveal (4.16 heard 4.14 Heat Integration Strategy). [`playbackNarrationKey`](src/lib/narrationAudio.ts) stashes tab audio as `tab:…`, never `slide:{id}`. [`slideTtsPatchAppliesTo`](src/hooks/useTTSGeneration.ts) does not stamp slide.voiceOverUrl from a tab job that still has `slideId`. Click-reveal rows are not tab TTS targets; leftover `tab:` blobs are not restored onto them.
- **A selected tab never plays Introduction.** [`playbackUrlForSlide`](src/lib/narrationAudio.ts) `tabExclusive` returns that tab’s clip or silence — not `slide.voiceOverUrl`. [`resolveTabForAudio`](src/lib/narrationAudio.ts) / [`ensureTabListIds`](src/lib/narrationAudio.ts) bind Add content tabs that were generated without ids. CC uses the tab Audio box, not the intro script.
- **Stolen copies are dropped.** [`unbindStolenSlideAudio`](src/lib/narrationAudio.ts) / [`unbindStolenNarrationRecords`](src/lib/draftMedia.ts) remove a slide-level clip whose URL or MP3 bytes match a tab on another slide. Load, save, and playback all run this. Do not play `restoredBySlideRef` if that blob is a tab clip.
- **A clip is bound to the Audio box.** TTS writes [`voiceOverClipText`](src/lib/narrationAudio.ts) (`stampSpokenClip`) with the script that was spoken. Playback refuses the URL when the box no longer matches. Empty Audio box → silence, even if a leftover MP3 is attached.

## How to change this

Change the helpers and add a failing test first. Do not “fix” drift by hiding the Audio box or delaying first preview.
